#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/build-system-verification.md:81
msgid ""
"The earlier `acc70f30` run [38280227545](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/actions/runs/38280227545) failed and remains failed evidence. Its "
"successful Native jobs do not qualify the failed aggregate run or this later"
" source. The fixes make scoped preparation receipts match actual selected "
"dependency closures, separate canonical-budget byte tampering from measured "
"authored-budget overruns, bind expected ThreadX link failure to the exact "
"Ninja ELF edge, and execute all four Python tool domains through the "
"maintained complete runner. Each fix retains real RED/GREEN execution and "
"independent review. The subsequent `3e7c0d50` run also failed: three Tool "
"Contract cases still addressed the removed GD32 helper. Its full raw "
"196-case execution remains failed evidence; `cc6a065c` restores the checked "
"contract entry point and retains the helper semantics. The final passing run"
" above must establish this correction separately."
msgstr ""
"The earlier `acc70f30` run [38280227545](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/actions/runs/38280227545) failed and remains failed evidence. Its "
"successful Native jobs do not qualify the failed aggregate run or this later"
" source. The fixes make scoped preparation receipts match actual selected "
"dependency closures, separate canonical-budget byte tampering from measured "
"authored-budget overruns, bind expected ThreadX link failure to the exact "
"Ninja ELF edge, and execute all four Python tool domains through the "
"maintained complete runner. Each fix retains real RED/GREEN execution and "
"independent review. The subsequent `3e7c0d50` run also failed: three Tool "
"Contract cases still addressed the removed GD32 helper. Its full raw "
"196-case execution remains failed evidence; `cc6a065c` restores the checked "
"contract entry point and retains the helper semantics. The final passing run"
" above must establish this correction separately."

